      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "LI T'ien-ching 李天經 (T. 仁常, 性參, 長德), 1579–1659, official, was a native of Wu-ch'iao, Hopei, descendant of a family of officials and scholars. His grandfather, Li I 李懿 (T. 省齋, chin-shih of 1544), served as intendant of the Hsi-ning Circuit, Kansu; and his father, Li Ju-fêng 李如峰 (西軒) held a post in the Banqueting Court.",
